# SRG-APP-000456-WSR-000187  -  CAT II
# The web server must install security-relevant software updates within 30
# days unless the time period is directed by an authoritative source (e.g.,
# IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, STIGs).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000456-WSR-000187
group:           V-206443
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002605
control_rev5:    SI-2

contribution:    Nothing toward installation: Splunk Web can be configured to check for new
                 vendor versions through web.conf [settings] updateCheckerBaseURL, or to
                 stop that outbound contact by setting it to 0, but the product has no
                 setting that acquires, schedules or applies a security-relevant update to
                 itself.

external:        The organization's flaw remediation procedure covering the Splunk Web
                 component of Splunk Enterprise, naming the authoritative source monitored
                 and the installation time period.
external:        The configuration management record of upgrades performed, which evidences
                 the period actually met.
external:        The vendor's supported release list, against which the installed version
                 and build are compared — the basis the attached product rule
                 SPLK-CL-000510 directs.
external:        The package or container image build and deployment pipeline that replaces
                 the installation, assessed against its own baseline; where
                 updateCheckerBaseURL is set to 0 for an enclave with no outbound vendor
                 contact, the authoritative source for update notice is carried entirely by
                 that procedure.

manual_reason:   Splunk Web is a component of the Splunk Enterprise installation and is not
                 separately patchable; it is updated when the whole installation is
                 replaced from a vendor-supplied package. The requirement's discussion
                 anticipates a web server configured both to check for and to install
                 security-relevant updates, and Splunk exposes the checking half only:
                 web.conf.spec:192 updateCheckerBaseURL causes Splunk Web to ping the
                 vendor for notice of new versions, and setting it to 0 stops that contact,
                 which is the value taken where outbound vendor contact is not permitted —
                 so the key records which authoritative source the procedure must monitor
                 rather than deciding the requirement, and it is not made a condition
                 because neither value installs anything. No key in the specification set
                 acquires, schedules or applies an update, and checks.tsv attaches no conf,
                 stanza or key to this requirement. Because the objective is the
                 installation of the update within a time period and the product provides
                 no installation mechanism, the determination rests on the installed
                 version and build compared against the vendor's supported release list,
                 and on the flaw remediation and upgrade record.

citation:        SRG-APP-000456-WSR-000187 check, fix and discussion text (CCI-002605, SI-2
                 c); attached product rule SPLK-CL-000510, whose fix text directs an
                 upgrade to a vendor-supported version and whose check text states the STIG
                 is sunset — no configuration setting is named. No conf, stanza or key is
                 attached to this requirement in the mechanism inventory. Splunk 10.x
                 specification set (Version 10.0.0): web.conf.spec:192
                 updateCheckerBaseURL, documented as the vendor URL Splunk Web pings for
                 new versions and settable to 0 to stop the ping — a notification control,
                 not an installer; app.conf.spec:116 show_upgrade_notification (app scope);
                 serverclass.conf.spec:316 updaterRunningFilter (deployment clients).
finding:         Splunk Web is not separately patchable and Splunk Enterprise provides no
                 setting that installs its own updates, so this requirement is not decided
                 by application configuration: a finding is raised only where the installed
                 version and build are no longer vendor-supported, or where the flaw
                 remediation record does not show security-relevant updates installed
                 within 30 days or within the period an authoritative source directs, and
                 it is recorded against the organization's flaw remediation process and the
                 installed software rather than against the Splunk application
                 configuration assessed here.
